# ---- Client ----
# Base URL of the DocExpire API, used only when the app is NOT served by the API.
#
# Leave this unset for the normal case: the server ships the built client and the
# API together, so the browser calls the same origin it was loaded from and needs
# no configuration at all. This is the right setting for every web deployment.
#
# Set VITE_API_URL only when the client and the API are on different origins:
#
#   * Mobile builds (Capacitor). A native WebView has the origin
#     capacitor://localhost, which has no API behind it, so a mobile build MUST
#     set this to your deployed HTTPS URL. Put it in client/.env.production:
#
#         VITE_API_URL=https://your-docexpire-service.onrender.com
#
#   * Local development against a Vite dev server. `npm run dev` serves the
#     client on :5173 and the API on :5000, and falls back to
#     http://localhost:5000 automatically, so this is optional there too.
#
# Never put a secret in this file. Anything here ships inside the JavaScript
# bundle and is readable by anyone using the app.
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
